@startuml How a finished render reaches the browser
title How a finished render reaches the browser\nMagic Hour's webhook and the browser's own polling race to the same shared finalize step

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User as U
participant "Browser\n(whichever page is open)" as B
participant "GET /api/history" as H
participant "Status check\n(runs after the response)" as R
participant "POST /api/webhook" as W
participant "Finalize\n(shared, claim-guarded)" as F
database "MongoDB" as DB
participant "Magic Hour" as MH

U -> B : press Transform
B -> MH : (via POST /api/transform) job submitted, saved as processing

== While the job is unfinished ==

loop browser poll: 3s -> 10s -> 30s\n(paused while the tab is hidden or the browser is offline)
  B -> H : GET /api/history
  H -> DB : read this user's jobs
  H --> B : job list + live counts\n(answered straight from the database)
  group after() : once the response is already sent
    H -> R : check this user's stale jobs
    R -> DB : pick at most 5 unfinished jobs\nnot already checked in the last 60s
    R -> MH : ask each one's status
    MH --> R : queued / rendering / complete / failed
    R -> DB : record the new phase
  end
end

== Whichever finishes first ==

alt Magic Hour's webhook arrives (the normal path)
  MH -> W : video.completed
  W -> W : verify HMAC signature + timestamp\n(fails closed - no secret, no action)
  W -> F : finalize(job)
else the webhook was lost, or none is reachable locally
  R -> F : finalize(job) - the status check saw "complete"
end

F -> DB : claim the job (status = finalizing)
note right of F
  The claim is exclusive: whichever path
  arrives second finds the job claimed
  and does nothing.
end note
F -> MH : fetch the rendered video's URL
F -> DB : store the result, status = complete\n(the file itself is copied into Cloudinary - see the storage diagram)

== Next poll ==

B -> H : GET /api/history
H -> DB : read
H --> B : the job is complete
B -> B : nothing live left -> stop polling
@enduml
